title: 'Fixes for issues reported by the Runtime Whitebox Fuzzer'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Fixed an integer overflow in `is_scheduling_parent_valid` when calculating the next slot
    for a leaf with slot `u64::MAX`. Slot calculation now uses checked addition.
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Fixed an off-by-one check in `pallet-elections-phragmen::submit_candidacy` that allowed
    one more candidate than `MaxCandidates`. It now properly rejects submissions when the limit
    is reached, returning `TooManyCandidates`. The corresponding benchmark component range was
    updated to `[0, MaxCandidates - 1]`.
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `pallet-conviction-voting`'s `Tally::add` and `Tally::remove` now compute all field updates
    before applying them. If an arithmetic overflow or underflow occurs, the tally remains
    unmodified and returns `None`.
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `cumulus_primitives_timestamp::InherentDataProvider::provide_inherent_data` now uses
    saturating arithmetic for slot and timestamp calculations, avoiding panics and integer
    overflows on large inputs.
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    The chain selection subsystem now uses saturating subtraction when calculating the prune
    cutoff timestamp in `PruneOnly` mode, preventing underflow if the clock is behind the prune
    delay.
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    `sc_consensus_slots::proposing_remaining_duration` now enforces the `max_block_proposal_slot_portion`
    cap across all execution paths, not only when slot lenience is applied.
- audience: [Runtime Dev, Runtime User]
  description: |-
    `pallet_scheduler::set_retry` now rejects named tasks with `Error::Named`. Callers must use
    `set_retry_named` to configure retries for named tasks, ensuring the task ID is properly included
    in emitted events. Existing retry configurations and `cancel_retry` remain unaffected.
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `pallet-nft-fractionalization::unify` now attempts to finish destroying the fractional asset
    upon unification, cleaning up asset metadata and freeing reserved deposits on the pallet account.
    If open accounts or approvals prevent immediate destruction, the asset remains in the destroying
    state without failing the `unify` call.
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `pallet-derivatives` now correctly emits `DerivativeMappingCreated` when registering a derivative
    mapping, rather than duplicating `DerivativeCreated`. The `DerivativeCreated` event is now only
    emitted once upon derivative creation.
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Widened intermediate calculations in `pallet-ranked-collective` to `u64` for `Linear` and `Geometric`
    vote-weight converters as well as `Tally::approval`. This prevents integer overflows when calculating
    vote weights or tally approval at `Rank::MAX` or with maxed votes.
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Fixed an issue where `dispute-coordinator` failed to shut down cleanly when receiving a `Conclude`
    signal before its first active leaf arrived. `initialize` now returns on `Conclude`, allowing
    the subsystem to exit cleanly.
crates:
- name: polkadot-collator-protocol
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-elections-phragmen
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-conviction-voting
  bump: patch
- name: cumulus-primitives-timestamp
  bump: patch
- name: polkadot-node-core-chain-selection
  bump: patch
- name: sc-consensus-slots
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-scheduler
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-nft-fractionalization
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-derivatives
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-ranked-collective
  bump: patch
- name: polkadot-node-core-dispute-coordinator
  bump: patch
